From: CJ Damsleth <kim@damsleth.no>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tps6598x: add SPMI transport for T6040 SN201202x

The Apple M4/T6040 generation carries its four Type-C USB-PD controllers on
Apple SPMI (compatible "usbc,sn201202x,spmi"), not on I2C like the M1/M2
"apple,cd321x" parts. The controller speaks the same TPS6598x logical-register
protocol (VID 0x00, STATUS 0x1a, the DATA1/CMD1 4CC pair 0x09/0x08, SSPS
system-power-state, ...), so the entire tipd state machine and cd321x_data
apply unchanged; only the register transport differs.

Factor the transport-independent bring-up out of the I2C probe into
tps6598x_probe_common(dev, regmap, irq, data) and a matching
tps6598x_remove_common(dev). The I2C driver becomes a thin wrapper; a new
SPMI driver (spmi.o, linked into the same tps6598x module) is registered
alongside it from a shared module_init.

The SN201202x does not expose its logical registers as a flat SPMI register
space, so devm_regmap_init_spmi_ext() -- which maps regmap register N onto
SPMI extended register N -- cannot drive it. The part is paged: a transfer
first selects the logical register by writing its number to SPMI register 0
(SPMI "Register 0 Write"), waits for the select register to read back that
number with its busy bit (BIT(7)) cleared, then transfers the payload through
a data window at SPMI register 0x20 in <=16-byte SPMI-extended chunks with the
window address auto-incrementing across chunks. A small regmap_bus reproduces
this paging so core.c keeps seeing a flat 8-bit map. The access mirrors
Apple's AppleHPMARMSPMI::readRegs and the m1n1 bring-up path proven live
against this hardware.

Bring-up only. TYPEC_TPS6598X_SPMI is a new bool depending on SPMI; the SPMI
probe does WAKEUP + (via cd321x_data.switch_power_state) SSPS-to-S0 and reads
only -- it issues no role-swap 4CC. Not submitted upstream as-is.

Signed-off-by: CJ Damsleth <kim@damsleth.no>
---
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Kconfig b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Kconfig
index b82715293072..d178d4c8fdac 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Kconfig
@@ -10,3 +10,17 @@ config TYPEC_TPS6598X
 
 	  If you choose to build this driver as a dynamically linked module, the
 	  module will be called tps6598x.ko.
+
+config TYPEC_TPS6598X_SPMI
+	bool "SPMI transport for the TPS6598x-family PD controller driver"
+	depends on TYPEC_TPS6598X
+	depends on SPMI
+	select REGMAP
+	help
+	  Add SPMI support to the TPS6598x driver, for the Apple M4/T6040
+	  generation whose four Type-C PD controllers (compatible
+	  "usbc,sn201202x,spmi") sit on Apple SPMI rather than I2C. The part
+	  speaks the same TPS6598x register protocol; only the transport
+	  differs. The SPMI transport is linked into the same tps6598x module.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Makefile b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Makefile
index aa439f80a889..21af8c502100 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/Makefile
@@ -3,4 +3,5 @@ CFLAGS_trace.o			:= -I$(src)
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_TYPEC_TPS6598X)	+= tps6598x.o
 tps6598x-y			:= core.o
+tps6598x-$(CONFIG_TYPEC_TPS6598X_SPMI)	+= spmi.o
